BACKUP ~weidu_external/JarnipToB/backup~
AUTHOR ~RZABON~
VERSION ~v1.0.0~

README ~JarnipToB/README.TXT~

ALWAYS


	DEFINE_ACTION_FUNCTION autotra_workaround BEGIN
	COPY ~JarnipToB/Languages/English~				~weidu_external/JarnipToB/Languages/autotra/%LANGUAGE%~
	COPY ~JarnipToB/Languages/%LANGUAGE%~				~weidu_external/JarnipToB/Languages/autotra/%LANGUAGE%~
	END

	LAF autotra_workaround END

	ACTION_IF GAME_IS ~bgee eet~ BEGIN
//  ACTION_DEFINE_ARRAY RL#_noconvert BEGIN END

		ACTION_DEFINE_ARRAY RL#_reload BEGIN Setup END

			LAF HANDLE_CHARSETS
				INT_VAR
				infer_charsets = 1
				STR_VAR
				tra_path = EVAL ~weidu_external/JarnipToB/Languages/autotra~
				out_path = EVAL ~weidu_external/JarnipToB/Languages/autotra/UTF8~
				iconv_path = ~JarnipToB/Languages/autotra/iconv~
				// noconvert_array = RL#_noconvert
				reload_array = RL#_reload
			END

	// Backup ANSI
	COPY ~weidu_external/JarnipToB/Languages/autotra/%LANGUAGE%~			~weidu_external/JarnipToB/Languages/autotra/ANSI/%LANGUAGE%~
	// UTF8 only
	COPY ~weidu_external/JarnipToB/Languages/autotra/UTF8/%LANGUAGE%~			~weidu_external/JarnipToB/Languages/autotra/%LANGUAGE%~
	END
END

AUTO_TRA ~weidu_external/JarnipToB/Languages/autotra/%s~

LANGUAGE ~English~
         ~english~
         ~JarnipToB/Languages/english/setup.tra~

BEGIN @100 /* Jarnip in ToB: A New Merchant in Saradush */
REQUIRE_PREDICATE (GAME_IS ~bgt soa tob bg2ee eet~) @101 /* Must be installed on BG2, BGT, BG2EE or EET */

// JARNIP'S DIALOGUE

COMPILE	~%MOD_FOLDER%/dialogue/JP#2.d~

// CREATURE: JARNIP

COPY ~%MOD_FOLDER%/creatures/JP#2.cre~ ~override~
SAY NAME1 @102 /* Jarnip */
SAY NAME2 @102 /* Jarnip */
WRITE_ASCII 0x2cc ~JP#2~ #8  // dialogue // WRITE_ASCII DIALOG ~JP#2~ (8)
WRITE_ASCII 0x248 ~JP#2~  #8  // override // WRITE_ASCII SCRIPT_OVERRIDE ~JP#2~ (8)
WRITE_ASCII DEATHVAR ~JP#2~ (32)

// STORE: JARNIP'S WARES

COPY ~%MOD_FOLDER%/store/JP#2.sto~ ~override~
SAY 0xc @103 /* Jarnip's Wares */ // SAY STORE_NAME

// SCRIPT: SPAWN JARNIP

EXTEND_TOP ~AR5003.bcs~ ~%MOD_FOLDER%/scripts/AR5003.baf~

// JARNIP'S ITEMS

COPY ~%MOD_FOLDER%/items~ ~override~

COPY ~%MOD_FOLDER%/items/JP#99.itm~ ~override~
SAY NAME1 @104 /* Bane of the Innocent +4 */
SAY NAME2 @104 /* Bane of the Innocent +4 */
SAY DESC @105 /* The first victims of this sword were not warriors. They were pilgrims. Peasants. Beggars. Those who could not fight back.

Long ago, this forsaken blade belonged to an unnamed holy champion who was suddenly stripped of his deity's grace. Instead of seeking penance, he chose the path of vengeance. It is said that the slaughter of the followers of his former faith was so great that the screams of his victims became permanently imbued within the blade.

Bane of the Innocent strikes terror into the hearts of those who face it and does not tolerate the touch of the righteous. Because of unspeakable atrocities committed with it in the past, only those who follow the path of the antipaladin, or who have become fallen paladins, can wield it.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Fire Resistance: +20%
- Characters of Good or Neutral alignment are slain upon equipping this sword

Combat abilities:
- Touch of Terror: 25% chance on hit to cause the target to panic for 4 rounds
- Dooming Presence: 5% chance on hit that all enemies within a 15-ft. radius panic and receive a -2 penalty to Armor Class, hit rolls, and damage rolls for 1 turn

THAC0: +4 
Damage: 2d4+4 (slashing), +2d4 (fire)
Speed Factor: 4 
Proficiency Type: Bastard Sword
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 10 Strength

Weight: 3 */

COPY ~%MOD_FOLDER%/items/JP#98.itm~ ~override~
SAY NAME1 @106 /* The Triumphant +5 */
SAY NAME2 @106 /* The Triumphant +5 */
SAY DESC @107 /* According to legend, The Triumphant first belonged to a barbarian king of Narfell who perished while defending his homeland from an invading horde of demons from the Endless Wastes. The sword was said to have been found on the battlefield after its wielder had single-handedly defeated an entire army. No body was ever found. Only the sword remained, lying amid the dead.

Since that time, The Triumphant has appeared in countless sagas of the northern barbarian tribes, becoming a powerful symbol of might and perseverance. Some say that whoever claims the sword is destined for greatness, while others believe that the blade simply finds those who are worthy of it.

Whatever the truth, those who take up The Triumphant soon discover that even impossible odds can be overcome.

STATISTICS:

Equipped Abilities:
- Strength: +2

Combat Abilities:
- Furious Strikes: Critical hits knock the target back and deal an additional 2d12 slashing damage
- Heroic Inspiration: While enraged, increases Armor Class by 2, Critical Strike chance by 5%, and grants an extra attack per round

THAC0: +5
Damage: 1d10+5 (slashing)
Speed Factor: 5
Proficiency Type: Two-handed Sword
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 16 Strength

Weight: 15 */

COPY ~%MOD_FOLDER%/items/JP#97.itm~ ~override~
SAY NAME1 @108 /* Herbert's Gauche +3 */
SAY NAME2 @108 /* Herbert's Gauche +3 */
SAY DESC @109 /* This off-hand dagger originally belonged to Herbert Schwarz, a famous Waterdhavian duelist whose adventures along the Sword Coast became a subject of innumerable folk tales. After retiring from adventuring, Herbert settled down in Calimshan and spent his final days surrounded by admirers and courtesans.

STATISTICS:

Equipped Abilities:
- Armor Class: +2
- Attacks per round: +1

Special Abilities:
- Casts Mirror Image two times per day

THAC0: +3
Damage: 1d4+3 (piercing)
Speed Factor: 0
Proficiency Type: Dagger
Type: One-handed
Requires:
 3 Strength

Weight: 1 */

COPY ~%MOD_FOLDER%/items/JP#96.itm~ ~override~
SAY NAME1 @110 /* Vigilant Eye +4 */
SAY NAME2 @110 /* Vigilant Eye +4 */
SAY DESC @111 /* Holy Shield of Protection: Vigilant Eye

This intricately decorated shield is forged from polished azure steel and bears the holy symbol of Helm. The blessing granted to it by the Vigilant One is truly incredible, as it extends beyond its bearer and protects all allies who stand beside the paladin.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Armor Class: +5
- Saving Throws: +1
- Magic Resistance: +10%
- Aura of Protection: All party members gain:
   +1 bonus to Armor Class
   +1 bonus to all saving throws

Requires:
 13 Strength
 13 Wisdom

Weight: 8 */

COPY ~%MOD_FOLDER%/items/JP#95.itm~ ~override~
SAY NAME1 @112 /* Bloodseeker Axe +4 */
SAY NAME2 @112 /* Bloodseeker Axe +4 */
SAY DESC @113 /* Rumors claim that this adamantine two-handed axe was crafted by the mad wizard Halaster Blackcloak for a berserker minotaur warlord who guarded the entrance to the Undermountain's main treasury. The creature was eventually slain by a band of adventurers, who claimed the axe as their prize. What became of the treasure itself remains unknown.

STATISTICS:

Equipped Abilities:
- Regenerate 1 Hit Point every 2 seconds

Combat Abilities:
- Thirst for Blood: Each hit deals an additional 4 points of slashing damage and heals the wielder for 4 Hit Points. On a critical hit, it deals an additional 15 points of slashing damage and heals the wielder for 15 Hit Points. This will not heal beyond the wielder's maximum

THAC0: +4
Damage: 1d10+4 (slashing)
Speed Factor: 5
Proficiency Type: Axe
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 17 Strength

Weight: 25 */

COPY ~%MOD_FOLDER%/items/JP#94.itm~ ~override~
SAY NAME1 @114 /* Light of Eldath +5 */
SAY NAME2 @114 /* Light of Eldath +5 */
SAY DESC @115 /* This unique greater Staff of the Woodlands was a personal gift from Eldath to the High Vychlaran of Rashemen. Blessed by the Green Goddess herself, the staff embodies her peaceful domain, granting an incredible blessing and calling upon the judgment of nature against anyone who dares to harm its wielder.

STATISTICS:

Equipped Abilities:
- Fire and Cold Resistance: +20%
- Armor Class: +2
- Saving Throws: +1
- Wisdom: +2

Combat Abilities:
- Emerald Rebuke: Any creature that strikes the wielder in melee must save vs. Wand at -2 or suffer 1d6+5 poison damage and become entangled for 4 rounds

THAC0: +5
Damage: 1d6+5 (crushing)
Speed Factor: 0
Proficiency Type: Quarterstaff
Type: Two-handed
Requires:
 10 Dexterity
 15 Wisdom

Weight: 4 */

COPY ~%MOD_FOLDER%/items/JP#93.itm~ ~override~
SAY NAME1 @116 /* Helm of the Broken Weave */
SAY NAME2 @116 /* Helm of the Broken Weave */
SAY DESC @117 /* Forged by dwarven smiths during an ancient war against the archmages of Netheril, this heavy helm is laced with veins of black meteoric iron that seem to drink in magical energy. Wizards standing nearby often describe an oppressive sensation, as though the Weave itself grows thin in its presence.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Armor Class: +1
- Magic Damage Resistance: +30%
- Protects against critical hits

Combat abilities:
- Anti-Magic Aura: Enemy arcane spellcasters cast spells at +2 casting time and suffer 25% spell failure (Wizard Slayer only)

Weight: 2 */

COPY ~%MOD_FOLDER%/items/JP#92.itm~ ~override~
SAY NAME1 @118 /* Cloak of the Crimson Abbot */
SAY NAME2 @118 /* Cloak of the Crimson Abbot */
SAY DESC @119 /* Long ago, this legendary cloak was a hereditary artifact worn by the abbots of the Monastery of the Crimson Rose in Shou Lung. After the monastery was raided and destroyed by the Tuigan Horde, the artifact was thought lost forever. How it eventually found its way to the Sword Coast remains unknown, but there is little doubt that it is one of the most powerful monk relics in the Realms.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Hit Points: +10
- Attacks per round: +1 (Monk only)

Combat abilities:
- Scarlet Palm: Each successful melee hit with fists has a 33% chance to stun the target for 1 round (save vs. Spell negates)

Weight: 4 */

COPY ~%MOD_FOLDER%/items/JP#91.itm~ ~override~
SAY NAME1 @120 /* Robe of Balagos +6 */
SAY NAME2 @120 /* Robe of Balagos +6 */
SAY DESC @121 /* This robe was crafted by the legendary red dragon Balagos to wear when he assumed human form. Later, Balagos gifted the robe to the leader of his human worshippers. Woven from heavy Calimshan silk and adorned with the scales of the great wyrm, it contains a fragment of Balagos's own draconic power. Only those touched by dragon blood can unlock the robe's full potential.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Armor Class: 4
- Decrease casting time by 2
- Physical Damage resistance: +30% (Red Dragon Disciple only)
- Fire damage dealt by the wearer: +20% (Red Dragon Disciple only)

Charge abilities:
- Casts Dragon Breath once per day
 Damage: 20d10 (Save vs. Breath for half)
 Area: 15-ft. radius
 Does not harm party members

Weight: 3 */

COPY ~%MOD_FOLDER%/items/JP#90.itm~ ~override~
SAY NAME1 @122 /* Torm's Gauntlets */
SAY NAME2 @122 /* Torm's Gauntlets */
SAY DESC @123 /* These gauntlets are said to have been worn by Torm himself during the Time of Troubles. Whether the legend is true or not, they grant the wearer a powerful blessing, strengthening their resolve and improving their divine spellcasting skills.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Armor Class: +1
- Saving Throws: +1
- Spell Casting Speed Improved by 2 (Clerics and Paladins only)
- Divine Casting Level: +1 (Clerics and Paladins only)

Weight: 1 */

COPY ~%MOD_FOLDER%/items/JP#89.itm~ ~override~
SAY NAME1 @124 /* Herbert's Coat of Fortune +5 */
SAY NAME2 @124 /* Herbert's Coat of Fortune +5 */
SAY DESC @125 /* This exceptional studded leather once belonged to Herbert Schwarz, a famous Waterdhavian duelist whose adventures along the Sword Coast became the subject of innumerable folk tales. Herbert was known for being able to escape from even the most dangerous situations, a talent he owed largely to this enchanted armor. Durable, lightweight, and enchanted with a permanent blessing of fortune, this armor is the dream of any adventurer.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Luck: +1 (Swashbuckler only)

Combat abilities:
- Avoid Death: When the wielder's Hit Points fall below 25%, grants 20 temporary hit points, +5 to saves vs. Death, and immunity to death magic for 1 round. This effect can only occur once every 1 turn.

Armor Class: 2 (0 vs. slashing, 1 vs. piercing and missile), 1 (Swashbuckler)
Requires:
 8 Strength

Weight: 10 */

COPY ~%MOD_FOLDER%/items/JP#88.itm~ ~override~
SAY NAME1 @126 /* Nethraval's Legacy */
SAY NAME2 @126 /* Nethraval's Legacy */
SAY DESC @127 /* Lesser Crown of Netheril: Nethraval's Legacy

This ancient and powerful artifact was forged during the height of the Netheril empire by the archmage Nethraval. It is said that crowns like this allowed Netherese arcanists to wield magic independently of the Weave, and even challenge and control deities. While this appears to be a lesser version of the Netherese crowns, the power it grants the wearer is beyond incredible.

STATISTICS:

Equipped abilities:
- Intelligence: +2
- Wisdom: +2
- Saving Throws vs. Spell: +2
- Spell Casting Speed Improved by 2 (Specialist Mages only)
- Arcane Casting Level: +2 (Specialist Mages only)

Weight: 1 */

